cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use skyplothelper in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "skyplothelper"
abstract: >
  Astronomy visualization toolkit: WCS frames, spherical geometry,
  tilted globes, and cone (z-RA) wedge frames built on top of
  matplotlib and astropy.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cigan"
    given-names: "Phil"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pjcigan/skyplothelper"
url: "https://github.com/pjcigan/skyplothelper"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-05"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - visualization
  - matplotlib
  - wcs
  - healpix
# A DOI / Zenodo / journal reference will be added in a later release.

references:
  - type: data
    title: "Outlines of the IAU Constellations"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Davenhall"
        given-names: "A.C."
      - family-names: "Leggett"
        given-names: "S.K."
    year: 1989
    notes: >
      Bundled IAU constellation boundary corners
      (skyplothelper/data/constellation_corners.npz) are sourced from
      this catalog (Vizier VI/49, table bound_18) and precessed from
      B1875 to ICRS with astropy. The underlying boundary definition
      is the IAU 1930 (Delporte) post-revision.
    url: "https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/VI/49"

  - type: data
    title: "d3-celestial — Constellation asterism lines"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Frohn"
        given-names: "Olaf"
    year: 2015
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >
      Bundled IAU asterism (connect-the-dots) line data
      (skyplothelper/data/constellation_lines.npz) is derived from
      d3-celestial's constellations.lines.json, which in turn is drawn
      from the IAU's Constellation page with minor line modifications
      and cleanup by Olaf Frohn. The IAU itself does not publish a
      single canonical asterism dataset distinct from the boundary
      definitions; this is the de-facto IAU-derived, BSD-redistributable
      reference.
    url: "https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial"

  - type: data
    title: "Natural Earth — coastlines, land, lakes, rivers, and time zones"
    year: 2024
    notes: >
      The Earth vector overlays (coastlines.npz, land.npz, lakes.npz,
      rivers.npz, and time_zones.npz) are NOT shipped with the package —
      they are generated on demand into a local cache by
      ``skyplothelper.prepare_earth_data()``, which downloads them from
      Natural Earth. Natural Earth is released into the public domain (no
      attribution is required; it is credited here as good practice). Time
      zones were donated to Natural Earth by International Mapping
      Associates, Inc.
    url: "https://www.naturalearthdata.com/"

  - type: data
    title: "PB2002 — global model of present-day plate boundaries"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Bird"
        given-names: "Peter"
    year: 2003
    doi: "10.1029/2001GC000252"
    notes: >
      The tectonic-plate polygons and boundaries (tectonic_plates.npz,
      used by ``plot_tectonic_plates``) are the PB2002 model of Bird
      (2003), "An updated digital model of plate boundaries"
      (Geochemistry, Geophysics, Geosystems, 4(3), 1027). Like the other
      Earth data they are NOT shipped with the package; they are fetched on
      demand by ``skyplothelper.prepare_earth_data()`` from the fraxen/
      tectonicplates GeoJSON redistribution (public domain).
    url: "https://github.com/fraxen/tectonicplates"
